\description{
\strong{Get the box score of one game from the live API: one row per player plus
each side's team-only and totals rows, with by-quarter scores, referees and
attendance repeated on every row.}

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://live.euroleague.net/api/Boxscore?gamecode=\{game_code\}&seasoncode=\{season_code\}}

\code{Stats} holds one object per side (\code{Team}, \code{Coach}, \code{PlayersStats}, \code{tmr} =
team-only rebounds, \code{totr} = totals). Each side's players become rows tagged
\code{row_type = "player"}, followed by the side's \code{"team"} and \code{"total"} rows.
Every row also carries the game's \code{attendance} and \code{referees} and, for the
row's side, \code{team_name}, \code{coach}, the points scored per quarter
(\code{by_quarter_q1} ...) and the cumulative score at the end of each quarter
(\code{end_of_quarter_q1} ...).
}
\details{
Unofficial, keyless API, not supported by Euroleague Basketball; hoopR only
wraps it (wrap-only: payloads are not redistributed as release assets). This
function mirrors its sdv-py twin of the same name: same arguments, defaults
and snake_case columns, one row per sdv-py row.

The live API's codes are space-padded fixed-width strings
(\code{TEAM = "IST       "}); every string cell is stripped. Its "no such game"
answer is an \strong{empty 200 body}, returned as a zero-row tibble with the
documented columns (not an error). A 404 raises \code{hoopR_no_data}, a 400 / 422
\code{hoopR_invalid_request}, any other failure \code{hoopR_fetch_error} (all inherit
\code{hoopR_error}).
}
